The [#4471 page](/kb/incidents/4471) says one issue, one fix queued. The reports merged into it
hold three problems, and each has a ticket of its own:

- **parser**, day-first dates read month first:
  [ticket #1](https://github.com/aleksej-axiology/support-kb/issues/1). Fixed by
  `fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales` when #4471 closed.
- **hint**, booking-v3 asks for the month first:
  [ticket #2](https://github.com/aleksej-axiology/support-kb/issues/2). Won't fix: the booking-v3
  form is retired.
- **one-day move**, the date shifts by a day:
  [ticket #3](https://github.com/aleksej-axiology/support-kb/issues/3). Open: neither change
  touches it.

## How many reports each covers

The desk's own view of #4471, built from its export at render time. `parser` and `hint` are its
rows. The one-day moves are its footnote: the desk files them under `parser` by tenant, so the
parser count includes them.

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

## parser: day-first dates read month first

The shared parser reads every date month first. A tenant whose locale writes the day first gets
its dates back with day and month swapped: "7 April" goes out as "4 July". This is the bug the
#4471 page describes, and the fix queued there was for this one.

## hint: booking-v3 asks for the month first

booking-v3 prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field and then reads the date the tenant's way, day
first. People booking a day-first tenant through that form type what the hint tells them. The
symptom is the same swap, so these reports read like `parser`, but the parser fix does not reach
them: the form's hint has to follow the tenant's locale. Only reports that came in through a
booking-v3 tenant's `form` channel have this cause.

## one-day move: the date shifts by a day

These are not swaps. "Tuesday 12 May" arrives as "Monday 11 May", a client in Lisbon gets Tuesday
while one in Toronto gets Monday, an invite arrives before the booking was made. The day moves and
the month stays, which points at time zones, not at the parser.

## How the reports were split

- One report per id. The export repeats some reports where its pages overlap.
- The cause comes from the tenant: its locale, its booking form, and the channel the report came
  in by (`causes.ts`). Intake's tag is not used: intake tags `hint` whenever the reporter's
  browser is en-US, whatever the tenant runs.
- The one-day moves are the desk's own reading (`desk-notes.json`), checked against every report
  body: they are the only reports whose dates are not a day/month swap.

## Lessons

- A subject line says what someone saw, not why. "Month and day swapped?" turns up under every
  problem here, one-day moves included, so matching on subjects cannot keep them apart.
- Count a merged ticket by cause before marking it known. One fix per ticket is a claim the
  reports can check.

